    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the number of ways Johnny can choose 3 marbles out of 7 different colored marbles. This is a combination problem, where the order of selection does not matter. The formula for combinations is given by:\n\n\\[ \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\]\n\nHere, \\( n \\) is the total number of items (marbles) and \\( k \\) is the number of items to choose. In this case, \\( n = 7 \\) and \\( k = 3 \\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using the `math` module which provides a function to calculate factorials.\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Number of marbles\nn = 7\n\n# Number of marbles to choose\nk = 3\n\n# Calculate the number of combinations\nnum_ways = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(num_ways)\n```\n```output\n35\n```\nThe number of ways Johnny can choose 3 different marbles from a bag containing 7 different colored marbles is \\(\\boxed{35}\\).",
