    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways Johnny can choose three different marbles from a set of 7 different colored marbles. This scenario involves options that can be represented by combinations (order does not matter).\n\nUsing the formula for combinations:\n\n[ C(n, k) = frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} ]\n\nWhere ( n ) is the total number of items in my marble bag, and 7 is 3 is the number of marbles I draw.\n\nSo the number of ways Johnny can choose three marbles from his bag is:\n\n[ C(7, 3) = frac{7!}{3!(7-3)!} = frac{7*6*5*4!}{3!4!} = frac{7*6*5}{3*2*1} ]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways Johnny can choose three marbles from a bag of seven colored marbles:\n\n[ 35 = frac{7*6*5}{6*5*3*1} = frac{7*6*5}{3*5*6} ]\n\nThis results in the number of ways:\n\n[ 35 = frac{7}{3*5/6} = frac{7}{5/3} = frac{7*3}{5} = frac{21}{5} ] ways.",
